{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And in the greatness of Your majesty.</b> This hand alone shatters the enemy — when He raises it in the greatness of His majesty, then He destroys those who rise against Him. And if in the greatness of His majesty alone His enemies are destroyed, how much more so when He unleashes wrath against them — it will consume them." "<b>You destroy.</b> You constantly destroy those who rise against You. And who are they, these who rise against Him? These are they who rise against Israel. And so it says: ״כִּי הִנֵּה אוֹיְבֶיךָ יֶהֱמָיוּן״ (Psalms 83). And what is this humming? ״עַל עַמְּךָ יַעֲרִימוּ סוֹד״ (ibid.) — and on this account He calls them His enemies, the enemies of the Omnipresent."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:52:19.515153823Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}